"""Forty independent complete original-field readings, before candidate inspection."""
NOTES = {}


def note(number, language, text):
    key = ('deenhindi-bukhari:' + number, language)
    assert key not in NOTES
    NOTES[key] = text


note('2469', 'hi', 'The Hindi-labelled field is Latin transliteration. Anas reports the month oath, upper room, Umar’s question, denial of divorce and return after29days. The inserted pre-ila5AH chronology is explanatory apparatus. I initially retain the ila-occasion setting and the actual moon-sighting parenthesis because they locate the exchange and supply the causal premise of is liye; these are source statements, not independently verified dates. All wording and distinct event framing remain literal.')
note('2469', 'ur', 'The Urdu fully supplies Anas’s oath/room/Umar dialogue and29-day return. The5AH pre-ila parenthesis is a chronological insertion. The ila occasion and moon-sighting cause appear to function as actual setting and causal narrative, unlike a lexical gloss; I initially retain them. The statement is reported source wording, not an independent chronology claim.')
note('2473', 'hi', 'This Hindi slot is Latin. Ikrama reports hearing Abu Hurayrah’s Messenger-attributed seven-hand road decision. I initially retain ki zameen as the actual disputed-property object, with the dispute condition and seven-hand measure intact. No modern unit conversion or wider rule is supplied.')
note('2473', 'ur', 'Ikrama/Abu Hurayrah explicitly attributes the road-dispute decision to the Messenger. The parenthetic road-land object appears to supply material scope for the disputed strip; preserve the conditional setting and seven-hand measure, without a modern measurement.')
note('2474', 'hi', 'The Hindi-labelled text is Latin. Adi’s hearing from Abdullah ibn Yazid introduces the actual Prophetic prohibition of looting and mutilation. The inline jo Adi bin Sabit ke nana thay is an explanatory chain-identity apposition, not an independently attributed report body; it can remain visible context. The two prohibitions are complete.')
note('2474', 'ur', 'The actual report is Abdullah ibn Yazid’s transmission of the Prophet’s two prohibitions. The inline maternal-grandfather relation describes the route identity and should be distinguished as context from that finite prohibition. Do not invent definitions of muslah or a missing event.')
note('2479', 'hi', 'This Hindi slot is Latin. Aisha’s curtain with pictures, the Prophet seeing/removing/tearing it, her making two cushions and his sitting on them are all supplied. The when-he-saw parenthesis is actual event sequence. The Aisha-ne-bayan-ki resumption identifies the subsequent first-person maker and is meaningful attribution, not a new Prophetic saying.')
note('2479', 'ur', 'The own Urdu supplies the entire curtain/cushions account. Preserve the actual seeing condition and the Aisha reporting resumption before the first-person cushion-making. The two cushions and later sitting are source events; no outside legal inference is added.')
note('2483', 'hi', 'The damaged opening omits much of the route and leaves only bin Abdullah before the expedition. Keep that defect rather than importing Urdu’s complete Jabir chain. The Rajab7AH insertion is apparatus; the whatever-rations-remain condition is operative. Wahb’s named first-person question to Jabir is a distinct voice in the same report. I initially retain the fish-body comparison qualifier as the physical basis of the mountain simile. Preserve the literal कहता typo,18nights and camel/rib account.')
note('2483', 'ur', 'The full Urdu route names Malik/Wahb/Jabir, unlike the shorter Hindi opening. Jabir’s expedition, remaining-rations order, shortage, fish and ribs are actual. The inserted Rajab7AH date is context. Retain the remaining-rations scope, the Wahb attribution at the intervening question and the physical-body comparison qualifier. Separate that question/reply from the resumed expedition voice without creating another transmitted occurrence.')
note('2485', 'hi', 'Latin text occupies the Hindi field. Rafi ibn Khadij explicitly describes praying Asr with the Prophet, slaughtering camel(s), dividing into ten shares and eating cooked meat before sunset. The complete timing and sequence are actual report content, with no compiler tail.')
note('2485', 'ur', 'Rafi’s own Urdu supplies the whole Asr/camel/ten-share/cooked-before-sunset sequence. All of it is attributed report content; do not add an inferred duration or normalize the source’s singular/plural wording.')
note('2489', 'hi', 'The Hindi-labelled Latin field reports Abdullah ibn Umar’s Prophetic prohibition of taking paired dates without companions’ permission. Dastarkhwan par supplies the shared-meal domain and should remain with the permission limitation; it is not a generic ban on eating dates privately.')
note('2489', 'ur', 'Abdullah ibn Umar explicitly attributes this prohibition to the Prophet. Preserve both the permission limitation and the shared-table setting, as well as the actual two-dates-at-once conduct. No additional legal rule is inferred.')
note('2494', 'hi', 'The full Hindi-labelled Latin field is Urwah’s inquiry and Aisha’s attributed explanation, not the Prophet’s speech. The actual supplied verse fragments, own translation and her orphan/mahr account are eligible under expanded sayings. Doosri sanad, Surah Nisa location and the wali kinship-definition list are apparatus. Retain the conditional permission apodosis toh is soorat mein nikah... and the later question’s explicit subject. No verse text or canonical locator is completed.')
note('2494', 'ur', 'I fully read the long Urdu inquiry/exegesis. Aisha’s own conditional account and interpretations are attributed sayings, with real quoted Arabic and supplied translations retained. The second-route label, explicit surah locator and guardian-definition examples are context. The parenthetic permission consequence completes her preceding condition; the later question-domain parenthesis identifies what was asked and remains. Keep Urwah’s framing separate from Aisha’s actual voice.')
note('2495', 'hi', 'This Hindi-labelled source is Latin. Jabir reports the Prophet’s shufa decision and its precise partition/boundary/road exceptions. The zameen-jaidad-waghera examples are a gloss on amwal rather than another report; keep them as context while retaining every actual condition. The printed Zubairi route is not corrected from another field or external edition.')
note('2495', 'ur', 'Jabir’s own Urdu preserves the unpartitioned-property decision and the termination once boundaries/roads are changed. The parenthetic land/property/etc examples explain the noun amwal and can remain context. Do not silently normalize the printed زبیری name or add a legal application.')
note('2496', 'hi', 'The Hindi slot is Latin. This separate Jabir occurrence supplies the complete common-property/shufa decision and its boundary/road exception, with no parenthetic explanation. Keep the whole actual report and distinct occurrence identity.')
note('2496', 'ur', 'The full Urdu supplies Jabir’s Prophetic decision on still-unpartitioned shared property and the complete boundary/road exception. No compiler tail occurs. It remains a distinct numbered transmission, not a duplicate merged with2495.')
note('2497', 'hi', 'Latin Hindi slot. Sulaiman asks Abu Minhal about a present transaction; Abu Minhal describes his unnamed partner and asks Bara, who recounts his own earlier transaction with Zaid and the Prophet’s actual cash/deferred reply. Preserve two distinct event families and actual voices. Both naqd parentheses merely gloss already stated hathon-hath and are context; no missing goods identity is invented.')
note('2497', 'ur', 'The own Urdu contains the later Abu Minhal transaction and the earlier Bara/Zaid episode with the Prophetic reply. They must remain distinct related report families within this source occurrence. Both نقد synonyms explain ہاتھوں ہاتھ and are context. Preserve the unnamed current partner, conditional permission/refusal and all source punctuation.')
note('2498', 'hi', 'This independently read Latin Hindi field literally repeats the supplied2497 wording, but its number and occurrence remain distinct. Keep the Abu Minhal and Bara/Zaid event families separate and the actual Prophet reply under its stated attribution. The two naqd synonym parentheses remain context; no cross-ID identity merge follows the equality.')
note('2498', 'ur', 'I read this whole Urdu field independently despite its equality with2497. It supplies two transaction episodes and their different speakers. Retain the actual permission/deferred refusal and both source families; the two repeated نقد glosses are context. Source identity remains2498.')
note('2499', 'hi', 'The Hindi-labelled Latin route names Abdullah without an added father-name. It reports the Messenger’s Khaybar land arrangement: work/cultivation and half the yield. The complete supplied terms are actual report content; do not infer an omitted Ibn Umar metadata identity.')
note('2499', 'ur', 'Nafi’s source route names Abdullah only. Keep the complete Messenger-attributed Khaybar arrangement, work/cultivation and half-yield term. No missing personal name, external contract classification or legal conclusion is supplied.')
note('2505', 'hi', 'The whole Hindi field supplies Ibn Abbas’s Hajj/umrah account, Jabir’s quoted objection and gesture, the Prophet’s sermon, Suraqah’s duration question and Ali’s later arrival/hadi instruction. The source’s compressed counterfactual remains literal. The answer नहीं के लिए है lacks the duration/object and should remain damaged context, not be repaired to Urdu’s always. Preserve distinct actual voices and every other supplied action.')
note('2505', 'ur', 'Ibn Abbas’s full Urdu includes the actual conversion-of-intention account, Jabir’s objection, sermon with both counterfactual clauses, Suraqah’s question/full always-answer, and Ali’s arrival/instruction. The قربانی gloss of hadi is context. Preserve full operative clauses, attribution and gesture; do not transfer this complete answer into Hindi.')
note('2506', 'hi', 'I fully read this distinct occurrence despite literal equality with2505 Hindi. Preserve the printed source narrative, voice changes, compressed conditional and Ali ending. The uncompleted नहीं के लिए है answer remains context with its missing duration explicit; no identical-ID or cross-language repair is permitted.')
note('2506', 'ur', 'This separately numbered Urdu occurrence contains the same full supplied Hajj/umrah dialogue and always-answer, which is independently admissible here. The قربانی noun gloss is context, while both actual counterfactuals and the complete Ali command remain. Preserve its own source identity.')
note('2508', 'hi', 'The Hindi-labelled field is Latin. Anas supplies three distinct reports: armor pledged for barley, his own bread/fat visit, and an expressly heard Prophetic statement about morning/evening household provisions. Separate those report families and keep the final third-person nine-houses fact as the reporter’s own framing, not as extra Prophetic words.')
note('2508', 'ur', 'The full Urdu contains the pledge, the first-person meal visit and the expressly heard household-provision saying. Those are separate reported events/utterance families. The final third-person nine-houses clause is actual narrative framing and must not be relabelled as the Prophet’s direct statement. Preserve the one-saa quantity without conversion.')
note('2513', 'hi', 'Aisha’s full printed chain supplies the Messenger’s grain purchase with a deferred period and armor pledge to a Jewish seller. The complete finite report is admissible as supplied, without an inferred period length, seller name or another source’s context.')
note('2513', 'ur', 'Aisha’s own Urdu supplies the whole deferred grain purchase and armor pledge. Keep the actual chain and unnamed Jewish seller, with no added timing, identity or transaction ruling. No compiler tail is present.')
note('2519', 'hi', 'Asma explicitly attributes the eclipse-time slave-freeing instruction to the Messenger. The later Musa/Ali ibn Madini/Darawardi/Hisham support-route sentences contain no new body and belong to transmission context. Keep the source’s printed Fatima-name form unchanged.')
note('2519', 'ur', 'Asma’s Urdu report expressly names the Messenger and the eclipse-time instruction. The final alternative-route support notice is apparatus, including its closing Hisham fragment. Do not turn that chain tail into a second narration or repair the source’s narrator spelling.')
note('2520', 'hi', 'Asma says they used to be commanded to free slaves during an eclipse. The passive issuer is not named in this own field; preserve an actual Companion report with an unresolved issuer rather than importing the explicit Messenger attribution from2519. All own wording is finite and supplied.')
note('2520', 'ur', 'This separately numbered Asma report uses a passive command during eclipses without naming who issued it. Keep that attribution gap and the actual repeated-practice content. No Prophetic name or canonical equivalence is transferred from adjacent source occurrences.')
note('2532', 'hi', 'Qais reports Abu Hurayrah arriving with a slave, intending Islam, and their accidental separation. The फिर यही हदीस pointer and comparison bridge are context. A later actual Abu Hurayrah saying makes the honorific-designated addressee witness that the slave is for Allah. Keep this as his own supplied saying, without inventing the omitted reunion or a missing explicit manumission verb.')
note('2532', 'ur', 'The own Urdu supplies the arrival/Islam intention/separation and a disjoint actual Abu Hurayrah witness statement. The intervening same-hadith pointer/comparison is context, not reconstructed story. Preserve the source’s honorific address and Allah-dedication wording under Abu Hurayrah’s voice, with the missing link unfilled.')

assert len(NOTES) == 40
